# Study prerequisite map — the zone-of-proximal-development gate for `/study`.
#
# Format:  <prereq-rung> <glob>      first match wins; blank lines and `#` ignored.
#
# The number is the rung a reader must ALREADY HOLD for the document to pay off —
# NOT the document's own rung on the capability ladder. The two differ, and
# conflating them is why the first version of `study-frontier.py` had no gate at
# all. The ladder (docs/development-timeline.md) tracks DEPTH OF ENGAGEMENT with
# the same object; L3 ("the system around the model") is not harder than L2, it is
# a different axis. What a menu must not do is offer a document standing two rungs
# of prerequisite above the reader — mechanistic interpretability at scale to
# someone whose attention derivation is still open.
#
# The gate shows a document when  prereq <= reader_rung + 1  (`.claude/study-reader-rung`).
# The "+ 1" IS the zone of proximal development: at your rung, or one above it,
# never two. An UNMAPPED document is never hidden — absence of data is not
# evidence of depth. Held-back documents are always reported as a count, never
# silently dropped (explicit n/a beats silent absence).
#
# Rung meanings are the ladder's: L0 math substrate · L1 derive the mechanism ·
# L2 how a real model is built · L3 the system around the model · L4 observe
# mechanism in a trained model · L5 measure across training · L6 predict and
# falsify · L7 build at scale.

